  "description": "LLM-inference accelerator block: a matrix unit (MXU), a vector unit (VPU), DMA between the slice DRAM and on-chip tensor memory, and an instruction sequencer, in SystemVerilog. The ASIC top (rtl/asic/otpu_asic_top.sv) is one slice and its collective unit with the slice's DRAM ports at the boundary (no memory controller or PHY inside). Upstream also ships an ISA, a bit-exact simulator, a kernel compiler and host software, and reports the design running int8 and 4-bit LLMs on a Kintex-7 PCIe card (self-reported, not verified by Vyges). The FPGA board glue (rtl/boards, generated LiteDRAM) is not mirrored. Mirror of FeSens/openTPU.",
